---
import Layout from "../layouts/layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Notes">
<html>
  <body>

    <h1>&#128216; League Notes</h1>

    <p>
      This page documents major league rule changes, scoring updates,
      terminology, and historical context that may affect statistical
      comparisons across seasons.
    </p>

    <h2>Scoring Eras</h2>

    <h3>2010 - 2020: Pre-PPR Era</h3>

    <p>
      Prior to 2021, the league did not use full Point Per Reception (PPR)
      scoring. As a result, offensive scoring was generally lower and season
      point totals from this era may not be directly comparable to later years.
    </p>

    <h3>2021 - Present: PPR Era</h3>

    <p>
      Beginning in 2021, the league adopted PPR scoring. This increased scoring
      league-wide, particularly for high-volume pass catchers.
    </p>

    <h2>Game Types</h2>

    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>Code</th>
        <th>Meaning</th>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>R</td>
        <td>Regular Season</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>P</td>
        <td>Playoffs</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>C</td>
        <td>Consolation / Placement Games</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Playoff Placement Games</h2>

    <p>
      The league tracks final standings through playoff and placement games.
      These games determine the final finishing order for all teams, not just
      the champion.
    </p>

    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>Final Seeding</th>
        <th>Game</th>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>Championship Game</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>3</td>
        <td>Third Place Game</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>5</td>
        <td>Fifth Place Game</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>Seventh Place Game</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>Ninth Place Game</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>11</td>
        <td>Eleventh Place Game</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Toilet Bowl Definition</h2>

    <p>
      A Toilet Bowl championship is awarded to the winner of the lowest
      placement game for a given season.
    </p>

    <p>
      Because league size has changed over time, the Toilet Bowl is not always
      the 11th-place game.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>12-team seasons typically use the 11th-place game.</li>
      <li>10-team seasons typically use the 9th-place game.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Historical Notes</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>League membership has changed over time.</li>
      <li>League size has varied between seasons.</li>
      <li>PPR scoring began in 2021.</li>
      <li>Additional rule changes may be documented here in future updates.</li>
    </ul>
  </body>
</html>
</Layout>